			"date": "2026-06-02T18:27:37.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> FWIW, both Marvel and DC have subscription services that give you access to nearly everything in their back catalog. If I were in your shoes, I'd pick one of them, prioritize books from that publisher and then pick off some indies in addition that you either buy or check out from the library. Then next year, maybe switch to the other publisher and do the same.</p><p>Given Watchmen and Dark Knight Returns are seminal, I'd probably start with the DC sub.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
